+# Jeryu TUI multi-repo scope design
+
+## Problem
+
+The current fleet bar renders every tracked repository left-to-right. That works
+for three repos, but it collapses once a workspace contains dozens of repos and
+families such as `veox-shared`, `veox-deploy`, `veox-nht`, and `veox-proofs`.
+Operators need one default cockpit that shows all work, then a fast way to narrow
+every pane to a repo family or one repo without losing runner-utilization context.
+
+## Scope model
+
+The TUI has one global scope:
+
+1. `All` — default. Every workflow, mission, release, approval, job, agent,
+   test, pool, cache, evidence, bug, secret, LLM, Git, and audit pane renders all
+   data.
+2. Family — any repo basename with a dash is grouped by the prefix before the
+   first dash. Examples: `veox-shared`, `veox-deploy`, and `veox-nht` become
+   `veox-*`. Family selection filters every pane to those repos.
+3. Repo — a single repository filter.
+
+The family key comes from the slug basename first, then alias as fallback, so
+short aliases like `shared` can still belong to `veox-*` when the slug is
+`neverhuman/veox-shared`.
+
+## Navigation
+
+- `Esc`: return to `All` from any selected family or repo.
+- Focus FleetBar, then left/right or `h/l`: move across `All`, families, and any
+  ungrouped repos. The bar is short because grouped repos no longer consume one
+  segment each.
+- `Enter` on a family: open the family detail overlay. The overlay lists child
+  repos by active/failed/recent order and confirms that family scope is active.
+- `Enter` on a repo: open the existing repo detail overlay.
+- Future follow-up: `/` search for repo/scope names and `Enter` inside a family
+  overlay to descend into child repos without returning to the bar.
+
+## Sorting
+
+All lists that represent work should be recent-first within the active scope:
+
+- Jobs: `received_at DESC`.
+- Runner feeds: `updated_at DESC` when multiple live feeds match the scope.
+- Repo families and repos in the fleet bar: active work first, then failures,
+  then latest run update.
+- Workflow PR rail: existing PR order, filtered by `repo_alias`/`repo_slug`.
+
+## Filtering contract
+
+Renderers must call `App::repo_filter()` or one of the scope helpers before
+drawing data. Data with no repo identifier is visible only in `All`, not inside a
+specific repo or family.
+
+Required identifiers by source:
+
+| Data | Identifier |
+| --- | --- |
+| Workflow PRs | `repo_alias` or `repo_slug` |
+| GitLab jobs | `project_id`, resolved through repo registry `project_id` |
+| Runner feeds | `project_id` plus optional `repo_alias`/`repo_slug` |
+| Pipelines | `project_id` |
+| Git/audit/evidence/cache | add repo slug/project id as migrations expose it |
+
+## Cache and data isolation
+
+No cache, runner workspace, or evidence namespace should be shared across project
+boundaries by default. The isolation key is:
+
+```text
+repo_scope_key = provider + ":" + slug-or-project-id
+```
+
+Use that key in:
+
+- runner working directories;
+- hot cache roots;
+- CAS object namespace metadata;
+- taint records;
+- evidence capsule paths;
+- log capture paths.
+
+Sharing across a family (`veox-*`) must be opt-in via registry policy, not an
+implicit consequence of family view filtering. A family scope is a UI aggregation,
+not a storage namespace.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- Starting the TUI selects `All` and shows all work.
+- Three repos named `veox-shared`, `veox-nht`, and `veox-warp` render as one
+  `veox-*` scope in the bar.
+- Selecting `veox-*` filters Workflow PRs, Jobs, runner feeds, and pipeline
+  matrices to those repos only.
+- Selecting an unrelated repo hides all `veox-*` jobs and PRs.
+- `Esc` always returns the UI to `All`.
+- Jobs are displayed most-recent first inside `All`, family, and repo scopes.
+- Cache/evidence/runner paths include repo scope keys so two projects do not
+  share mutable data accidentally.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+cargo test -p jeryu --lib repo_fleet
+cargo nextest run -p jeryu -- tui::repo_fleet_bar tui::runtime::input::navigation
+cargo run -p jeryu -- tui --demo --tab jobs --once
+```
+
+Add screenshot tests for:
+
+1. default `All` scope;
+2. family `veox-*` overlay;
+3. repo-only scope;
+4. empty scoped jobs.
